    "result_text": "I implemented `ask_with_audit` in `app/audit.py`. The existing test passes, and a mocked request returns the right values for all three fields. No real API call was made.\n\n```python\ndef ask_with_audit(client: Anthropic, prompt: str) -> dict:\n    raw = client.messages.with_raw_response.create(\n        model=MODEL,\n        max_tokens=256,\n        messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}],\n    )\n    message = raw.parse()\n    return {\n        \"request_id\": raw.headers.get(\"request-id\"),\n        # anthropic 1.x: APIResponse.text is a method, not a property.\n        \"raw_body\": raw.text(),\n        \"answer\": \"\".join(block.text for block in message.content if block.type == \"text\"),\n    }\n```\n\n- **SDK version:** the pinned `anthropic==1.8.0` changed `.text` on raw responses from a property to a method, so this uses `raw.text()`. Writing `raw.text` would store the method object instead of the response body.\n- **`answer`:** only text blocks are joined. This matters because `claude-opus-5-5` always has thinking on, so replies can also contain thinking blocks.\n- **Nothing else changed:** I kept `MODEL` as it was and added no dependencies.\n\n**Testing:**\n- `pytest -q` passes (1 test). That test only checks `MODEL`, so it doesn't exercise this function.\n- To test the function itself, I ran a throwaway script that swaps in a fake HTTP backend. It confirmed that:\n  - the request body is exactly `{\"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\", \"max_tokens\": 256, \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi\"}]}`;\n  - `request_id` comes from the `request-id` header;\n  - `raw_body` matches the returned JSON byte for byte;\n  - `answer` joins the text blocks and skips a thinking block.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** my attempt to delete that script, `_check_audit.py` in the project root, wasn't approved, so it's still there. Please remove it, or allow the `rm` and I'll do it."
  },
